                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>I, Theopold Drouette, fifth justice of the peace for the parish of Orleans, do
                    hereby certify, before God, that Mr. George Turin, the signer and subscriber of
                    the foregoing affidavit, has exhibited unto me—</p>
                <p>1st. The consul certificate of her Britannic Majesty, testifying to his quality
                    of British subject; and, 2d. The certificate that he has taken the oath required
                    ‘from every foreign subject by General Order, No. 41.</p>
                <p>[SEAL.]</p>
                <p>[Stamp.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>T. DROUETTE, <hi rendition="#italic">Fifth Justice of the
                        Peace.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
